  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1137 PM CDT SUN OCT 25 2026\n\nNo major changes are expected in the forecast over the next five\ndays, as upper-level ridging is expected to remain in place\nthrough Wednesday. This will result in relatively stable\ntemperatures, and limited rain chances under this super dry air\ncolumn. By Thursday, this ridge will finally begin to break down,\nas a weak closed low moves into the central Plains. Here, our\nflow aloft will transition to the SW, allowing for some slight\nmoisture return in the upper-levels. At the surface however,\nwinds will remain from the E/NE, keeping dewpoints low into the\nweekend. With that being said, temperatures will slightly\nincrease under this new flow regime, with afternoon highs\nclimbing into the upper-70s and low-80s by Friday.\n\n/44/",
